# PowerStation — the org.shadowblip.PowerStation D-Bus service OpenGamepadUI's performance menu
# talks to (CPU core count, GPU clock range). Built FROM SOURCE via the local PKGBUILD: the holo
# snapshot has no powerstation, and upstream's aarch64 release cannot see an SoC GPU at all.
#
# The two patches are ours and are meant for upstream (ShadowBlip/PowerStation); drop each one
# when a release carries it:
#   0001  CPUs without SMT (every arm64 part) reported SmtEnabled=false, so SetCoresEnabled and
#         OGUI both halved the core count; and cores were grouped by topology/core_id, which on
#         big.LITTLE repeats per cluster. Groups by thread_siblings_list instead.
#   0002  A devfreq backend for GPUs that are not PCI devices (Adreno under msm): clock limits,
#         min/max range and the manual switch on /sys/class/devfreq/*.gpu; plus power profiles
#         (power-saving / balanced / max-performance = CPU schedutil / ondemand / performance,
#         GPU simple_ondemand / simple_ondemand / performance) on the TDP interface, and a core
#         brought back online takes cpu0's governor (an offline policy refuses the write).
#   0003  CoresEnabled returned before the cores moved (tokio File::write_all without a flush), so
#         back-to-back calls raced and an older "offline" could win, and 0002's governor copy ran
#         while the core was still offline. Awaits the write. Upstream bug, worth sending.
name: powerstation
pkgbuild_local: PKGBUILD
patches: 0001-fix-CPU-do-not-halve-the-cores-of-CPUs-without-SMT.patch 0002-feat-GPU-support-devfreq-scaled-GPUs-that-are-not-PC.patch 0003-fix-CPU-return-from-set_online_async-once-the-core-h.patch 0004-fix-CPU-keep-the-fastest-cores-online-first.patch
pkgrel_suffix: 1
